[thinking]
The bug: for an even number of elements, it should take the average of the two middle values. Fix:

```python
def median(xs):
    """Return the median of a non-empty list of numbers."""
    s = sorted(xs)
    n = len(s)
    mid = n // 2
    if n % 2 == 1:
        return s[mid]
    return (s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2
```

